> - *Infrastructure:* the files listed in DEV's `deploy\INFRA_MANIFEST.ini` (one path a line under `[files]`; first written
>   with the phase 2 package and reviewed; afterwards the owner adds or removes a line by hand), when
>   `deploy\INFRA_IS_INSTALLABLE.json` matches them. `Make_Installable.bat INFRA` writes that marker: the manifest
>   itself, every file it lists and every file of the install tool, with SHA-256. A listed file that does not exist
>   refuses.
129a134,138
> **3.4 Helpers are never updated in place (owner).** No command overwrites an installed helper, proved harmless or not.
> A wrong helper is handled in DEV: `Who_Uses.bat` finds the variants that declare it; `Make_Successors.bat` prepares
> a successor folder for each, pointing at the corrected file; the owner reviews, marks the batch, and installs it in
> the ordinary way; he withdraws the old variants in the tree and unmarks them in DEV (example 7).
> 
318a328,335
> 7. **A wrong helper.** `_shared\recurrence_gaps_v1.py` is found to be wrong. `Who_Uses.bat _shared\recurrence_gaps_v1.py`
>    lists twelve variants in four families. The owner writes `recurrence_gaps_v2.py` and runs
>    `Make_Successors.bat _shared\recurrence_gaps_v1.py _shared\recurrence_gaps_v2.py`: twelve new, unmarked folders
>    (`RECUR_MEAN_ALL_V2` beside `RECUR_MEAN_ALL_V1`, and so on). He reviews them, marks the batch, and runs
>    `Install.bat PROD`: twelve variants and one helper are added; nothing installed is touched. He withdraws the
>    twelve old variants in PROD with one command and one confirmation, and unmarks them in DEV. The next research job
>    fills the successors' history; the old variants keep their records up to the withdrawal.
